Changelog: 29-10-2026 13:03:08

Fixed. At the top or bottom of a list in a pane (Your games, the settings, the memory cards, the browser) the focus
jumped back to the cards on the left; it stays in the pane now, and only B goes back (owner, 29-10-2026; core's fix).

Changelog: 29-10-2026 12:46:22

Breaking. The app never starts a game (owner, 29-10-2026: the games are played from Steam, never in the emulator from
the app): A on a game is its Steam mark (X before), and nothing plays it from Your games.

Breaking. No pills (owner, 29-10-2026: one way everywhere): every action is in the row at the bottom, A too. The
PCSX2 pane: A Install, X Choose BIOS, Y Reinstall or Update, LB Remove BIOS and RB Remove PCSX2 (a second press each,
where they were pills); the Log pane: A View log (or a tap on the pane) shows the whole log in the app, the d-pad
scrolls it, B goes back (it opened in Notepad, which no button closes); the key page: A Save; the memory cards: A
Saves.

Fixed. A game folder and the BIOS dump could not be chosen with the controller (owner, 29-10-2026): Windows' own
folder and file windows are replaced by the app's browser (core's browse): + Browse to a folder… in Folders (A opens
a folder, B goes up, X adds the open one), and X Choose BIOS opens it in Downloads showing the .bin and .rom dumps (A
on one takes it). The information texts name the buttons ("the A button") and no longer say a game plays from the
app.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 11:35:27

Breaking. The buttons (owner, 29-10-2026: "Close" on B was not clear): B goes back (from a pane to its card, from a
page to where it came from; on a card it does nothing), View (⧉) exits the app and Menu (☰) opens the information of
the pane that shows; B on the folders goes back to the games, on a card's saves to the cards, on Steam artwork to
Your games. Exit asks first while PCSX2 is being downloaded or Steam changed (Press View again). The row at the
bottom ends with ☰ Info, B Back and ⧉ Exit app.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 11:04:36

Fixed. The PCSX2 pane's text showed through Steam artwork, Your games or another pane (owner, 29-10-2026), after
RB Steam artwork from a game in the list: two pages were visible at once. Core's fix: one page shows.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 06:24:25

Release 1.0.1.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 04:49:00

Release 1.0.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 04:28:23

Added. The Settings pane has tabs, with more of PCSX2's settings (owner, 29-10-2026: "we have way too less settings
in PCSX2, we can use tabs in the settings page to add more. Screen sizes should be added in the first page"): LB and
RB step through Picture (Renderer, Resolution up to 8x with the screen size each gives, Aspect ratio, Video aspect
ratio, Widescreen patches, Anisotropic filtering, VSync), Game (Fast boot, No-interlacing patches, Cheats, Save state
when quitting, Volume), Controller (Vibration, Stick dead zone, Stick range, Player 2, Quit with View + Menu) and On
screen (Show FPS, speed, resolution, CPU and GPU use, frame times, inputs, Text size); a tap picks a tab. The
information icon tells the tab's settings. Quit with Select + Start is named Quit with View + Menu, the handheld's
buttons.

Fixed. An action with a controller button is in the legend at the bottom alone (owner, 29-10-2026: "we have update
steam 2 times, in a orange button and at the bottom again"), and a tap on the legend's entry does the same: Your
games has X Steam mark, Y Update Steam, LB Folders (LB Games in the folders), RB Steam artwork; Memory cards X New
card and Y Copy card; the PCSX2 pane X Choose BIOS and Y Reinstall or Update; the key page X Paste and Y Remove key
(Y Press again for the second press). The pills that stay are Remove BIOS, Remove PCSX2, A Install, A Save and A
Open the log.

Fixed. Update Steam reads Steam's file back right after writing it, while Steam is still closed (owner, 29-10-2026:
"Update Steam does not seem to work it still says 0 games in steam"), and counts from that rather than from a read
once Steam starts again; a game written but not found then is named on the status line and in the log, with how
many of the app's games Steam's file names, so the log tells whether the file or the reading is at fault. The
shortcuts' fields are read whatever their case (Steam has written appname and exe in lower case in some versions),
and a failed read of Steam's file is logged instead of passed over.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 03:26:16

Release 1.0.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 02:41:27

Fixed. The PCSX2 pane's pills are one row (owner, 29-10-2026): Choose BIOS, Remove BIOS, Remove PCSX2, Y Reinstall
or Update, and A Install only while PCSX2 is not installed; the Your games pill is gone, as Your games is the card
on the left. A on the PCSX2 card, once installed, goes to the pills. The cards' column is narrower, so the row fits
at 1280 x 720 and 1097 x 617.

Fixed. No pill is grayed out any more (owner, 29-10-2026: "Update Steam button is not orange, Copy card button is
not orange"): Update Steam, Copy card, Choose BIOS, Remove BIOS, Remove key and the settings stay amber, and
pressed when they cannot act they say why on the pane's status line.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 02:21:23

Fixed. Y in Your games did nothing when there was nothing to do (owner, 29-10-2026): it says why on the status line now, with nothing marked to change, without Steam on the device, or with the folders shown. Y Remove key without a key says so too.

Fixed. The same pills in every pane (owner, 29-10-2026): amber, the same size, in a row at the bottom right with the A pill rightmost; the PCSX2 pane has Choose BIOS and Remove BIOS above Remove, Y and A. The games, the folders, the memory cards and the settings are rows; the focused one is lighter with the amber edge. Once the focus moves into a pane, the pane has the amber edge and glow and its card keeps the edge.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 01:50:35

Added. The suite's wallpaper behind the cards, as in the portal (owner, 29-10-2026), on or off with the
portal's Settings.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 01:48:33

Breaking. PCSX2's own window is never opened (owner, 29-10-2026: "we don't want to see PCSX2 at all, the manager
should take care of everything", the BC250 suite's rule): Open PCSX2 is gone (once PCSX2 is installed, A on the PCSX2
card goes to Your games), and so is the Big Picture setting, PCSX2's own menu; the app now keeps Big Picture off
([UI] StartBigPictureMode = false). A game starts with pcsx2-qt.exe -nogui -fullscreen -batch -- <game>, from the app
and from Steam's shortcuts (Update Steam rewrites them): -batch closes PCSX2 when the game ends. PCSX2 gets the
app's environment without Qt's own variables (with them, PCSX2 stopped with "no Qt platform plugin could be
initialized", seen on the Ally). No game starts without a BIOS: PCSX2 would stop at its own Startup Error window.

Added. The BIOS on the PCSX2 card's pane, as the BC250 app's BIOS Install and BIOS Uninstall (owner, 29-10-2026:
"where do I set the BIOS"): a BIOS row with the dump PCSX2 uses ("No BIOS yet" with why, also on the PCSX2 card),
Choose BIOS (Windows' own file window, in Downloads, *.bin and *.rom) copies the dump with the files beside it under
the same name into PCSX2's bios folder and names it in [Filenames] BIOS, Remove BIOS takes it out with its files on
a second press; both off while PCSX2 is not installed or runs. The information icon says where a BIOS comes from
(your own console, biosdrain, PCSX2's BIOS page).

Added. The SteamGridDB key, as the BC250 app's Steam artwork… (owner, 29-10-2026: "exactly as BC250 has it"): a
Steam artwork pill on Your games opens a page with the BC250 dialog's text, the key's field (masked), X Paste from
the clipboard (the key copied in a browser on the device), A Save and Y Remove key with a second press, B back.
One key for the suite, %APPDATA%\windows-portable-suite\steamgriddb-key, sent only to SteamGridDB; empty or removed
looks nothing up and the pictures kept stay in use. Told as the BC250 app tells it: "The SteamGridDB key was
changed." or "... taken out; the pictures kept stay in use." The wiki has a chapter for it, Steam artwork.

